                </h2>
                <p class="size-18" style="color: rgb(145, 145, 145);">Onyinyechi’s work sits at the critical intersection of bioethics, public health, and historical justice. She investigates how legacies of exploitation, medical racism, and inequality influence present-day healthcare delivery particularly in the areas of women’s health and reproductive justice. Her studies examine not only clinical outcomes but also lived experiences, narratives, and structural barriers that persist in underserved communities, both locally and globally.
